    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d909">

                <pb facs="1079" n="983" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg983"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-07-01"><hi rendition="#italic">July 1,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 725.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I confirm the Department’s telegram of the
                    29th ultimo, which deciphered reads as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Inform British Government of report that Spanish fleet intends to coal
                            from British colliers at island of Perim.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William R. Day.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
